 "notes": "Single map sheet read from OCR (page 1); most of the OCR text is map graphics. Map symbols are garbled or missing ('[ aFpas |', 'Pps') and were not recorded. The Water unit was not recorded. Legend-only features (contact, drill-hole symbol) were not recorded as values. Two thicknesses printed with '|' for a digit are read as 1, flagged inferred and sent to review. The OCR text ends at the scale bar; the base-map and datum block is not in it.\nSUBSURFACE: margin elevations: Holocene terrace sediments below 10 ft landward; Princess Anne Formation above 12 ft seaward, below 18 ft landward; Pamlico Formation above 17 ft seaward, below 25 ft landward (page 1). Beach sand lies above mean low water up to the storm tide line (page 1). The legend shows SCGS drill-hole locations with log identification numbers (e.g. 26-332), logs on file at the SCGS and not in this document (page 1). No cross sections or structure contours appear in the OCR text. Datum: not stated in the OCR text.",
